cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReviewMind in your research or educational work, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewMind: Hotel Review Sentiment Classification with TF-IDF and Multinomial Naive Bayes"
authors:
  - family-names: "Benyakoub"
    given-names: "Mohammed Ryad"
    email: "ryadbenyakoub@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RYAD-BENYAKOUB/ReviewMind"
url: "https://github.com/RYAD-BENYAKOUB/ReviewMind"
abstract: >-
  ReviewMind is an open-source text data mining and natural language processing
  project designed for hotel review sentiment classification. It features an
  end-to-end pipeline using TF-IDF feature extraction, hyperparameter-tuned
  Multinomial Naive Bayes, robust data preparation, and a dual-annotator human
  consensus framework for external generalization assessment.
keywords:
  - natural-language-processing
  - text-mining
  - sentiment-analysis
  - machine-learning
  - tf-idf
  - naive-bayes
  - scikit-learn
  - hotel-reviews
license: "MIT"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"

